      "Title: ServiceNow Change Request Filter UI Pitfalls\nDescription: Key observations and potential failure points when building complex filters on the Change Request list.\n- The filter panel is controlled by the 'Show / hide filter' toggle (bid a47).\n- Field choosers (e.g., a1181) use a combobox pattern to select filter fields.\n- Value choosers (e.g., a1639) may require `select_option` if clicking the option fails.\n- 'Add AND Condition' buttons (e.g., a1303) dynamically add the next filter row.\n- Operators are selected via a separate combobox (e.g., a2579 for 'is empty string').\n- Text inputs (e.g., a2118 for 'Requested by') accept direct text entry.\n- The filter div is identified by `change_requestfilterdiv`.\n- The filter logic defaults to AND ('All of these conditions must be met').\n- Specific fields like 'Model' require specific operators like 'is empty string'.\n- Focus management is critical when opening new condition fields.\n- Some actions may require specific focus handling (e.g., comboboxes).\n- The workflow requires sequential addition of conditions to build the full filter criteria."
